  // === crypto-dca ===
  "Mastering Dollar-Cost Averaging (DCA) in Volatile Markets": "La méthode DCA (Dollar-Cost Averaging) sur les actifs numériques",
  "Dollar-Cost Averaging is an investment discipline where you invest fixed cash sums at regular calendar intervals, eliminating the emotional pitfalls of market timing.": "Les cryptomonnaies connaissent une forte volatilité. Le DCA consiste à investir un montant fixe à intervalles réguliers pour lisser son prix de revient sans stress.",
  "Why DCA Tames Severe Volatility": "Lisser la volatilité grâce aux achats programmés",
  "In hyper-volatile asset classes like cryptocurrency, attempting to time market peaks and troughs often leads to panic selling at bottoms and FOMO buying at tops. DCA automatically acquires more units when prices crash and fewer units when prices surge, systematically lowering your average cost basis.": "Investir 50 € par semaine permet d'acheter davantage de jetons quand le marché baisse et moins quand il flambe, optimisant le coût d'achat moyen.",
  "Average Cost Basis Formula": "Formule du prix de revient unitaire moyen (PRU)",
  "The harmonic mean math of dollar-cost averaging ensures that your average purchase price is always lower than the simple arithmetic average of the market's fluctuating spot prices.": "Neutralise l'impact d'un mauvais point d'entrée exécuté au sommet d'une bulle spéculative.",
  "DCA Operational Best Practices": "Principes de gestion du risque",
